From b0f3266508f1b6ace39ba260328fc2d4dbad540b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:16:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Run font test in CI, cache gate scripts, fold tone marks in
 search
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- CI: add requirements-dev.txt (fontTools, brotli) and install it in both
  workflow jobs; test_site_symbols now fails instead of silently skipping
  when CI=true and the packages are missing.
- Dictionary/translator lock screens: build_site.py writes content hashes
  into each gate's ASSET_VERSIONS, replacing per-visit Date.now() cache
  busting. Unbuilt checkouts keep the timestamp fallback.
- Site search: inline, above-syllable and ASCII forms of a tone mark
  (ˋ ˎ ` / ˆ ꞈ / ˊ ˏ / ˉ ˍ) now match each other; the mapping is tested
  against content_harmonisation.UPPER.

No dictionary data, orthography or content changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BXPT66w1ApxGZnjD2tHA4A
